   "text": "I registered Lucia Ferreira as a new patient, and she now has a dashboard with patient ID 4. The duplicate check before saving found no existing matches. After saving, the dashboard header shows her name and DOB 1984-11-03; I didn't re-open the Contact tab to read the saved address, phone and email back.\n\nI entered these values:\n- **Name and DOB:** first name Lucia, last name Ferreira, date of birth 1984-11-03.\n- **Sex:** Female.\n- **Address:** 18 Pine Avenue, Springfield, Massachusetts, 01108.\n- **Phone and email:** home phone 413-555-0173 and l.ferreira@example.invalid in the Contact Email field.\n\nTwo things went beyond a literal reading of the task:\n- The form also has a required Birth Sex field, separate from Sex, and it blocked saving while empty. I set it to Female as well.\n- At the start I clicked \"Ask again later\" on the OpenEMR product registration popup so I could reach the Patient menu.\n\nRESULT: DONE patient ID 4 (Lucia Ferreira)",
